# Cargo build output. Multi-GB, fully regenerable, and rewritten on every
# build — never committed. (Nothing ignored this while the crate lived under
# code-coordinator's tui/ either, which is why `coord status` reported every
# fresh coord-tui checkout as dirty the moment it was registered, #2899/#2954.)
target/

# #1973 opt-in local co-development override: a copy of
# cargo-config-local-quadraui.toml.example, pointing the quadraui dependency
# at a local ~/src/quadraui checkout instead of the pinned git rev.
#
# It is machine-local BY DEFINITION — committing it repoints every clone's
# quadraui dep at a path that exists on exactly one box. Both this repo's
# CLAUDE.md and the example file itself already describe this path as
# "git-ignored"; until this file existed it simply was not, because the
# extraction (#2899) left the new repo with no .gitignore at all.
.cargo/config.toml
